cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the AI Runtime Evidence Protocol (AIREP), please cite it as below."
title: "AI Runtime Evidence Protocol (AIREP)"
abstract: >-
  A neutral, vendor- and model-independent protocol that separates AI runtime-governance
  evidence into four correlated artifact families: Decision, Control, Execution and Effect.
  Deterministic wire and integrity construction supports offline checking; bounded Core,
  Authenticated and Witnessed assurance concerns provenance, integrity and freshness rather
  than event truth; and lifecycle reconciliation preserves failure, missing, not-evaluated and
  indeterminate states. v0.2.0-beta.1 is an experimental, not-stable implementation target with
  a first-party four-family producer. No same-version third-party v0.2 producer-to-consumer
  interoperability result has been established.
